# ObfuScope end-to-end workflow on the OSPool, orchestrated by DAGMan.
#
#   condor_submit_dag obfuscope.dag
#
# Stages:
#   CORPUS    : N sharded Tigress generation jobs (corpus.sub). Each produces
#               one tarball of obfuscated C artifacts plus a JSONL manifest of
#               every attempt.
#   FEATURES  : N sharded feature-extraction jobs (features.sub).
#   MERGE     : concatenate shard CSVs into a single feature table (merge.sub).
#   GATE      : corpus health checks (gate.sub). Blocking.
#   GRID      : the embarrassingly-parallel experiment grid (experiment.sub),
#               expanded from grid.txt by make_manifest.py in the PRE script.
#   AGGREGATE : reduce per-cell JSONs into tables and figures (aggregate.sub).
#
# Edges enforce data dependencies; within a stage, jobs run concurrently subject
# to the access point's throttle.
#
# Why GATE sits before GRID
# -------------------------
# GRID is the expensive stage. A corpus whose classes carry no within-class
# variation yields saturated metrics that read as a strong result, and the
# defect is invisible in row counts, class balance, and grouped cross
# validation alike. Checking corpus health after the grid means retracting a
# number; checking it here means rebuilding a corpus. GATE therefore returns
# nonzero on a degenerate corpus and DAGMan holds GRID and AGGREGATE back.
#
# Running without CORPUS
# ----------------------
# To reuse an already staged corpus, comment out the CORPUS job, its PRE and
# POST scripts, and the PARENT CORPUS CHILD FEATURES edge, then move the
# package_src.sh PRE script onto FEATURES.

JOB   CORPUS     corpus.sub
JOB   FEATURES   features.sub
JOB   MERGE      merge.sub
JOB   GATE       gate.sub
JOB   GRID       experiment.sub
JOB   AGGREGATE  aggregate.sub

# Package current source before the first stage submits, so every job in the
# run (CORPUS, FEATURES, MERGE, GATE, GRID, AGGREGATE all
# `tar xzf obfuscope_src.tar.gz`) ships identical, up-to-date code without a
# separate manual step.
SCRIPT PRE  CORPUS  package_src.sh

# Merge the shard tarballs into one corpus tree, stage it to the OSDF path
# features.sub reads, and report the per-transformation generation yield.
SCRIPT POST CORPUS  assemble_corpus.sh

# Build grid.txt before the GRID stage is submitted.
SCRIPT PRE  GRID  generate_grid.sh

PARENT CORPUS    CHILD FEATURES
PARENT FEATURES  CHILD MERGE
PARENT MERGE     CHILD GATE
PARENT GATE      CHILD GRID
PARENT GRID      CHILD AGGREGATE

# Retry whole stages a few times to ride out transient OSPool preemption.
# GATE is deliberately absent: its failures are properties of the corpus, not
# transient faults, so a retry would repeat the same verdict at the same cost.
RETRY CORPUS    2
RETRY FEATURES  3
RETRY GRID      2

# Throttle simultaneously-idle jobs submitted to the schedd.
CONFIG dagman.config
